366	/// openai-node `ChatCompletionStream`: choices and tool calls are SPARSE arrays by index;
367	/// `id`, `type`, `function.name` and `custom.name` are REPLACED when truthy; `arguments` is
368	/// appended when not null, `custom.input` when truthy. A legacy `function_call` object is taken as
369	/// is, then its name replaced and its arguments appended. `finalChatCompletion` raises when a
370	/// choice has no `finish_reason` or no `role`, a tool call has no `type`, or a name or arguments
371	/// are missing. The SSE layer stops at `[DONE]` and raises on an `error` event or a truthy
372	/// `error` field.
373	/// SOURCE: openai-node <not pinned: modelled only>, src/lib/ChatCompletionStream.ts
374	/// #accumulateChatCompletion and finalizeChatCompletion; src/core/streaming.ts Stream.fromSSEResponse.
375	pub fn run_openai_node(bytes: &[u8]) -> Run {
